        "content": "#include <algorithm>\n#include <cstdint>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <vector>\n\nnamespace {\n\nconstexpr std::uint32_t MOD = 1000000007U;\n\nclass FastInput {\n    static constexpr std::size_t BUFFER_SIZE = 1 << 16;\n    char buffer_[BUFFER_SIZE];\n    std::size_t position_ = 0;\n    std::size_t length_ = 0;\n\n    char next_char() {\n        if (position_ == length_) {\n            length_ = std::fread(buffer_, 1, BUFFER_SIZE, stdin);\n            position_ = 0;\n            if (length_ == 0) return '\\0';\n        }\n        return buffer_[position_++];\n    }\n\npublic:\n    int read_int() {\n        char c = next_char();\n        while (c <= ' ' && c != '\\0') c = next_char();\n        int sign = 1;\n        if (c == '-') {\n            sign = -1;\n            c = next_char();\n        }\n        int value = 0;\n        while (c >= '0' && c <= '9') {\n            value = value * 10 + (c - '0');\n            c = next_char();\n        }\n        return value * sign;\n    }\n};\n\ninline std::uint32_t add_mod(std::uint32_t a, std::uint32_t b) {\n    const std::uint32_t sum = a + b;\n    return sum >= MOD ? sum - MOD : sum;\n}\n\n} // namespace\n\nint main() {\n    FastInput input;\n    const int n = input.read_int();\n    const int m = input.read_int();\n    if (n <= 0) return 0;\n\n    std::vector<std::uint64_t> blocked;\n    blocked.reserve(static_cast<std::size_t>(m));\n    const std::uint64_t width = static_cast<std::uint64_t>(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < m; ++i) {\n        const int y = input.read_int();\n        const int x = input.read_int();\n        blocked.push_back(static_cast<std::uint64_t>(y) * width + static_cast<std::uint64_t>(x));\n    }\n\n    std::sort(blocked.begin(), blocked.end());\n    blocked.erase(std::unique(blocked.begin(), blocked.end()), blocked.end());\n\n    std::vector<std::uint32_t> dp(static_cast<std::size_t>(n), 0);\n    dp[0] = 1;\n\n    std::size_t obstacle = 0;\n    for (int row = 0; row < n; ++row) {\n        const std::uint64_t row_start = static_cast<std::uint64_t>(row) * width;\n        const std::uint64_t row_end = row_start + width;\n        const std::size_t row_first = obstacle;\n        while (obstacle < blocked.size() && blocked[obstacle] < row_end) ++obstacle;\n        const std::size_t row_last = obstacle;\n\n        std::size_t at = row_first;\n        if (at < row_last && blocked[at] == row_start) {\n            dp[0] = 0;\n            ++at;\n        }\n\n        int column = 1;\n        while (at < row_last) {\n            const int blocked_column = static_cast<int>(blocked[at] - row_start);\n            for (; column < blocked_column; ++column) {\n                dp[static_cast<std::size_t>(column)] = add_mod(dp[static_cast<std::size_t>(column)], dp[static_cast<std::size_t>(column - 1)]);\n            }\n            dp[static_cast<std::size_t>(blocked_column)] = 0;\n            column = blocked_column + 1;\n            ++at;\n        }\n        for (; column < n; ++column) {\n            dp[static_cast<std::size_t>(column)] = add_mod(dp[static_cast<std::size_t>(column)], dp[static_cast<std::size_t>(column - 1)]);\n        }\n    }\n\n    std::printf(\"%u\\n\", dp[static_cast<std::size_t>(n - 1)]);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
        "path": "src/solution.cpp"
      }
    ],
    "hypothesis": "Replacing the dense obstacle matrix with sorted row-major obstacle coordinates and processing obstacle-free row segments makes the hot DP loop touch only the contiguous DP row, eliminating the per-cell obstacle load and avoiding O(N²) obstacle storage while preserving dense-DP work.",
    "notes": "This also handles N=1 and duplicate blocked-coordinate records correctly.",
